### 3️⃣  Enable CORS with a Whitelist

```bash
npm i cors
```

```js
const cors = require('cors');

const corsOptions = {
  origin: ['https://example.com', 'https://api.example.com'], // add your real origins
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true, // if you need cookies
  optionsSuccessStatus: 204,
};

app.use(cors(corsOptions));
```

> *Why?* Prevents certain types of Cross‑Site Request Spoofing and also protects the rate of access from unknown origins.

