| **CORS** | Not configured – could allow open CORS if you later use a frontend | `app.use(require('cors')({ origin: 'https://trusted.example.com', credentials: true }));` | Restricts who can call your API from a browser. |
| **Rate‑limiting** | None – easy for DoS/credential‑guessing | ```js\nconst rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');\nconst limiter = rateLimit({ windowsMs: 15*60*1000, max: 100 });\napp.use(limiter);\n``` | Limits how many requests a single IP can make in a time window. |
| **Body parsing** | Not required now, but future proof | `app.use(express.json());` | Gives you `req.body` for future POST/PUT endpoints. |
| **Input validation** | The `/users` endpoint always returns a static list – no validation needed now, but in any future endpoint you’ll want to sanitize and validate | `express-validator` or `joi`; e.g.: <br>`app.post('/users', check('name').isString().trim(), ...)` | Prevents XSS/SQL‑Injection when user input is stored or displayed. |
| **Error handling** | No global handler – app will crash on an unhandled exception | ```js\napp.use((err, req, res, next) => {\n  console.error(err.stack);\n  res.status(err.status || 500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });\n});\n``` | Ensures the server continues running and doesn’t leak stack traces to clients. |
| **Unhandled Promise rejections** | Unhandled rejections crash the process | ```js\nprocess.on('unhandledRejection', (err) => {\n  console.error('Unhandled Rejection', err);\n  // You can decide whether to exit or just log.\n});\n```. | Makes the app resilient against async bugs. |
| **Graceful shutdown** | App never listens to SIGTERM / SIGINT | ```js\nconst server = app.listen(...);\nconst shutdown = () => {\n  server.close(()=>process.exit(0));\n};\nprocess.on('SIGTERM', shutdown);\nprocess.on('SIGINT', shutdown);\n``` | Prevents orphaned connections or incomplete in‑flight requests when the container / host stops the process. |

